1
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:14,180
I'm on a journey out to see the world.

2
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:17,160
While I'm on my own, I've
yet to reach the end.

3
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,840
So won't you come along with me right now?

4
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:23,777
Surely then we can!

5
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:26,780
Follow me now as we
journey on from sea to sea.

6
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:32,220
For that treasure known
by everybody as One Piece.

7
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:37,440
Even though they laugh and
say it's just a fantasy.

8
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,857
We are going, there's no doubt we go.

9
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:45,180
Cause we can feel the
rush of energy overcome.

10
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:48,280
It will lead the way.

11
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,500
Keep pretending that you know what to do.

12
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:57,397
Books will only get in the way.

13
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:00,000
No guides for today.

14
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:02,437
Do not worry soon.

15
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,997
The rain will be gone with the wind.

16
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:05,717
Keep your chin up, raise the anchor.

17
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:06,630
Now that's what you'll do.

18
00:01:06,713 --> 00:01:07,777
Give it time and calm.

19
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,297
The storm that you have built within.

20
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,397
Come and have my board at number two.

21
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:13,537
Once tomorrow's wind picks up.

22
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:14,777
We set stuff cause we can't.

23
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:15,897
Thresh it up, stand tall.

24
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:17,277
And take a look at one of you.

25
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,657
All the journey makes
me want to see somebody.

26
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,681
There are things out there
you just won't believe.

27
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,760
Beyond your wildest dreams.

28
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,297
Don't think for a second.

29
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:30,780
It's not the truth.

30
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:32,797
That's the story.

31
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:34,717
Most will believe.

32
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,037
Not me.

33
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,400
Come and see.

34
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:40,757
I am on a journey.

35
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:42,317
Out to see the world.

36
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,317
Don't all on my own.

37
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,317
I've got my group of friends.

38
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,357
Together we've got our way.

39
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,957
That's how it's done.

40
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,017
Says your captain.

41
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,277
Who says it can't be done.

42
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,937
We haven't even tried.

43
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:55,937
Gotta just believe we'll
make it to the end.

44
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,577
I just wanna do it all right now.

45
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,817
Together surely we can.

46
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,717
Yes, we can.

47
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,097
You can.

48
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:06,737
Just take this moment in.

49
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:08,057
We can.

50
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:09,437
I can.

51
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,157
Just take this feeling in.

52
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,477
Right now.

53
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:14,900
Right now.

54
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:18,720
Oh yes, we can.

55
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:37,767
I can't find any documents related
to their trafficking deals.

56
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:38,840
Too convenient.

57
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:41,774
Obviously, somebody made off with them.

58
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:43,300
I thought as much.

59
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,777
It's the same story on my end.

60
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:50,017
All the weapons and explosives that were
left behind disappeared just as quickly.

61
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:51,924
It was no small amount, either.

62
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,980
The Navy was panicked, too.

63
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,798
Must have been a large organization.

64
00:02:57,340 --> 00:02:59,120
Like the Revolutionary Army?

65
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:00,800
That seems likely.

66
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,692
Anyway, it's time to go.

67
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,110
Palik.

68
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,957
Quite the nuisance, aren't they?

69
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,780
I couldn't agree more, boss.

70
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:11,040
Almost as irksome as you. Ha-hoo!

71
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:12,490
Wow!

72
00:03:12,573 --> 00:03:13,712
Sticking it to him, huh?

73
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:22,800
Now the question is, where
is Straw Hat going next?

74
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,580
This is a land of tragedy.

75
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:35,360
One that was beset by dark strings,
pulling its history in woeful directions.

76
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:38,737
And when the tragedies
piled up too high to count,

77
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:43,080
what could they do but drown out
their sorrows with the sound of music?

78
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:51,300
The sound of guitar, of feet
stomping, of hands clapping.

79
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:05,040
Until at last, the curtain
falls on this long performance.

80
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:06,760
A tragedy with no name.

81
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:11,120
As the music goes silent,
the truth rings out clearly.

82
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:22,380
The king has returned, and the path it
stretches out before them is one of peace.

83
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:25,980
I would like to propose
a suggestion to everyone.

84
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:27,860
All right.

85
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:31,120
I suppose that's the
cue to introduce myself.

86
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:33,520
I'm Gancho, Chief Donut.

87
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:38,800
Standing next to me here is my daughter.

88
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,700
My name's Moncherry.

89
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:47,220
She's so cute!

90
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:53,860
You want us to make this?
Is that right? Yes, please.

91
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:55,740
It's a real important job.

92
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:03,720
The Referee World Summit is this year.

93
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,100
It's coming soon, too.

94
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,094
We'd better get ready.

95
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:10,064
Can't be left behind, you know?

96
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,417
Father, good news.

97
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:16,917
Rebecca said she'll be stopping by early
this afternoon to cook some lunch for us.

98
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,300
Is that so? And Course?

99
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:21,440
Actually, he's coming too.

100
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:23,060
Well, that's wonderful.

101
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,997
Seems we'll have the whole
family together again.

102
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:27,280
It's been a while.

103
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,400
In the future,

104
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:33,137
those who come to visit
this kingdom will be

105
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:36,102
met with a surprise like
none other in the world.

106
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:40,977
Can I get a hat?

107
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:42,720
Would you look who it is?

108
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,600
Rebecca and Monterey.

109
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:52,660
Alongside the humans of the city, Tiny
Tomtata can be found living and thriving.

110
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:56,880
Hey, shouldn't we focus on
building houses first? No way!

111
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,708
This is our first priority.

112
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:04,520
Such an adorable sight may turn
into a tourist attraction itself.

113
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:14,480
This is a kingdom of love,
passion, and fairies.

114
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:17,740
I guess the statues are
important too. That's right!

115
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:20,800
Dress Rosa.

116
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:33,796
Once we finish transporting the
prisoner, I'll be heading on a journey.

117
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:34,850
A journey?

118
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:40,940
I can't set foot inside
any Navy base. Remember?

119
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:44,700
Not unless I turn in Straw Hat and Law.

120
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,100
You're so stubborn.

121
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:53,576
All you have to do is apologize and
then Sakazuki can save face easily.

122
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:54,821
I don't want to.

123
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:56,800
And why not?

124
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,120
Because I want to save face too.

125
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:06,880
Right, fine. Well...

126
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:13,360
Oh, Fujitora.

127
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:19,157
I'm telling you, Tsuru,
that man's an idiot.

128
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:21,887
He had one last chance
to do the right thing.

129
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:24,197
To side with me and eliminate all of those

130
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,751
brats before they caused any more trouble.

131
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:29,011
Now look at where we are.

132
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:33,620
I was holding the reins, you know.

133
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:38,220
The reins on all the monsters
that threaten this world.

134
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:42,100
Taking me down was a terrible mistake.

135
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,320
Just you wait.

136
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:47,020
You'll regret this decision soon enough.

137
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:51,589
Do you really believe the crap
that comes out of your mouth?

138
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:54,737
Don't be so delusional.

139
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:58,397
Everything would have worked out if
only we'd helped you, is that it?

140
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:00,940
Well, we didn't, so you can deal with it.

141
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,840
It's over and you lost.

142
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:16,556
Wow, you really aren't going
to give an inch, are you?

143
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,700
It takes a thief to know one.

144
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:24,608
So what do you think will happen
to the world of pirates now?

145
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:28,920
Let me answer that question
with one of my own.

146
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,997
What do you think happens
to monsters once they've

147
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:35,077
lost their source of food
and are off their leashes?

148
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:38,860
Is there anyone who rules these
seas who can reign them in?

149
00:08:39,140 --> 00:08:43,620
Who possesses the most power, the
most influence in these waters?

150
00:08:44,140 --> 00:08:46,140
One of the four emperors, perhaps?

151
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:49,360
Or the seven warlords
who struck a clever deal?

152
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:53,540
Maybe the brats from the
worst generation running wild?

153
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,320
Not quite.

154
00:08:58,140 --> 00:09:03,180
After all, we can't ignore the Navy,
swinging around their hammer of justice,

155
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:06,537
or the formidable fighters
of the Revolutionary Army.

156
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:09,540
who struggle fearlessly
for the common man.

157
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:16,080
Or will those with the will of D
walk in the shadows of history?

158
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:19,700
When and where will they
decide to show themselves?

159
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:24,237
Who's gonna side with who?

160
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:27,197
Who will betray who?

161
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:30,677
I have a message for you
to give the celestial.

162
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:36,177
Dragons in Marie Joie tell them they
will be dragged from their gilded halls.

163
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:42,077
It's been 25 years since gold Roger
conquered the Grand Line and no one's

164
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:47,637
done it since his rival White Beard
stood before the throne but met his end,

165
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,297
having never sat upon it.

166
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,957
So what happens now?

167
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:55,317
You think there are more pirates
running wild out there than ever before,

168
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:57,637
but there's just one empty seat.

169
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:59,797
You get it now.

170
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:04,997
All those pirates are about to

171
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:07,080
have a struggle for supremacy.

172
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,160
The mask is burning!

173
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:14,640
Put it out!

174
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:23,480
Are we headed to Impel Down?

175
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:26,016
In that case, I have a small request.

176
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:29,160
I need you to bring me
a newspaper every day.

177
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:32,660
Then at least I'll never be bored.

178
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:40,740
Looks like four Navy ships, but it's wild.

179
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:45,597
They've got so many heavy hitters,
even though this is just a transfer.

180
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,504
That's enough strength
to crush a whole country.

181
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:51,189
They're not taking
chances with Doflamingo.

182
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,940
Ah, bad news, Master Jack.

183
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:57,077
Looks like we can't get Joker.

184
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,060
Should we turn around? What?

185
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:03,062
Don't tell me what I can't
do, you piece of crap!

186
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:06,300
Who the hell do you think I am?

187
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:17,400
I don't like this at all.

188
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:20,277
It's like your ship has more
Luffy on it than ours does.

189
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:22,713
I'm so flattered that it stinks so well.

190
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:23,999
Are you listening?

191
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:27,865
There's something on this ship
more exciting than anything else.

192
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:32,940
And this fever cod here
is showing us the way.

193
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:35,940
It's the real Mr. Luffy.

194
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:42,620
It's truly an honor to
have you here, Mr. Luffy.

195
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:46,040
I never imagined my wildest
dreams would come true.

196
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:50,840
He's shining so brightly I can't even see.

197
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:53,414
It's a real struggle, I gotta tell you.

198
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,540
They're all families, huh?

199
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:04,937
Funny how everything worked
out with the Vivre card.

200
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:06,997
I guess we have Sabo to thank for that.

201
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:09,477
All right, this is a fever card of Luffy.

202
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:11,277
I had one made up, huh?

203
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,720
When did that happen?

204
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:16,637
I'll be taking a piece
as well, hell yeah! Mrs.

205
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:17,817
Sabo is the man!

206
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:19,397
He's the perfect big brother.

207
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:24,677
Strong and nice—listen, Luffy!

208
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:27,397
I'm not gonna be your
follower like the rest.

209
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,310
But

210
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:30,157
I'll take a piece just in case.

211
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:33,537
Okay, fine by me; should
be enough for everyone.

212
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:34,450
Looks

213
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:37,677
like it's farewell for now.

214
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,437
We'll meet again soon, boss!

215
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:41,057
No doubt in my mind.

216
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:42,777
Until next time—Straw Hat!

217
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:45,577
See you guys. Good luck.

218
00:12:45,660 --> 00:12:46,740
Man, that

219
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:50,717
was one heck of a party, huh?

220
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:53,377
Those guys really grew on me, Bartholomew!

221
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,037
Stop wasting time!

222
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:55,950
wasting time

223
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:57,910
Huh?

224
00:12:57,993 --> 00:12:59,424
I don't take quarters from you.

225
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,260
We should hurry.

226
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:04,140
Of course! On it, Mr. Zoro!

227
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:06,980
You heard the man! Straight for Zo!

228
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:08,180
Full speed ahead!

229
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,520
Yes, sir!

230
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:13,577
I wonder if the rest of the crew
made it safely to the island.

231
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:16,457
Nami was with them, so I know
they didn't lose their way.

232
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:19,599
But if Big Mom catches them,
that could be bad news.

233
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:20,860
It worries me.

234
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:22,800
Hey, Luffy.

235
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:26,537
I'm reading the paper, and it looks
like our bounties just went up.

236
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:27,450
Huh?

237
00:13:27,533 --> 00:13:28,960
I want to see it! Oh, yeah?

238
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:30,808
I thought you already knew!

239
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,657
Incidentally, I have
your posters in my room.

240
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:38,260
Come this way! Hooray!

241
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:40,377
You were ready for this, huh?

242
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:44,800
I threw yours away, but your
bounty's up to 500 million. Yeah?

243
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:46,041
Thanks, I guess.

244
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:48,558
I don't really care about that crap.

245
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:53,760
Now, gaze upon your own glory!

246
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:55,480
You framed them?

247
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:58,157
Yeah, along with the
autographs you gave me.

248
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,740
Shall we begin?

249
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:05,460
First of all, Straw Hat
Luffy, 500 million berries.

250
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:08,980
Yeah, I'm getting up there.

251
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:15,900
Next up is Pirate Hunter
Zoro, 320 million berries.

252
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:17,630
Nice.

253
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:19,437
Can we celebrate with a drink?

254
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:25,857
demon child nico robin
130 million berries.

255
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:28,637
Oh my, it's gone up!

256
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:34,117
cyborg Franky 94 million berries.

257
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:36,357
So close to a hundred!

258
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:39,397
Also, that's general Franky, not me.

259
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:41,617
Go on! Who's up?

260
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:43,700
200 million. Ha!

